# Applies wherever a Docker build context includes the repo root.
# Once backend/ and frontend/ are scaffolded, add matching per-folder
# .dockerignore files (bin/obj for backend, node_modules/dist for frontend)
# scoped to each service's own build context.

.git/
.github/
.idea/
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.angular/
*.md
!README.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The publish output carries every appsettings file it finds. A release build never reads these two
# — they sit behind #if DEBUG — but the file would still ship inside the image with the credentials
# readable, so keep them out of the build context in the first place.
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/*.local.json
